# exceptions.txt — opt out of notifications from channels you're SUBSCRIBED to.
#
# Your watchlist is your YouTube account's subscriptions (read automatically).
# This file is optional and only ever *removes* notifications — leave it empty
# to be notified about everything you're subscribed to.
#
# Tip: you can also add these from Telegram — send the bot /except and pick the
# channel and opt-out with buttons. It appends lines here (tagged with the
# channel name in a comment).
#
# One rule per line, in one of these forms:
#
#   <channel>                    mute the channel entirely (no notifications)
#   <channel> = videos           ONLY regular videos   (mute livestreams/premieres)
#   <channel> = livestreams      ONLY livestreams      (mute regular videos)
#
# <channel> can be any of:
#   @handle
#   https://www.youtube.com/@handle
#   https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
#   UCxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx        (raw channel ID)
#
# Lines starting with # are ignored. Examples (remove the # to activate):
#
# @SomeNoisyChannel                  # never notify me about this one
# @NewsNetwork = videos              # skip their 24/7 livestreams, keep uploads
# @MyFavoriteStreamer = livestreams  # only ping me when they go live
